{{Quote|"Let's kick a few butts!"<br>"Actually, most of the Galvan species are known as technological geniuses."<br>"Oh. Then let's outthink a few butts!"|[[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as Grey Matter and [[Professor Paradox]].<ref>''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref>}}
Grey Matter's small size masks his great calculative and technical intellect. He can create extremely advanced machinery from spare parts, understand the function of any device at a glance, and make sophisticated repairs to complex machines (such as a warp-drive engine).<ref name="Rad">''[[Rad]]''</ref> In fact, when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] becomes Grey Matter, he instantly knows more about the [[Omnitrix]]'s inner workings, including its malfunctions;<ref name="ASP">''[[A Small Problem]]''</ref> how to rectify it being tampered with; and how to remove its limiter (the latter two being demonstrated by [[Ben 23]] as [[Brainfrog]]<ref>''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]''</ref> and [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]] as Grey Matter,<ref name = "Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref> respectively.)

Grey Matter's intellect serves as a problem solver and analytical help in difficult situations. This allows Grey Matter to think more strategically when brute force is inefficient. He is also generally knowledgeable; even if he does not know something, he can learn it very quickly.{{Refn|[[:File:Grey Matter Can Learn Things Quickly.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Grey Matter's brain capacity also gives him an intuitive understanding of things he has never even seen before, like [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]]'s alien circuitry.{{Refn|[[:File:Grey Matter Brain Capacity.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref>''[[Hunted]]''</ref> Grey Matter's multidisciplinary intellect can also extend to understanding unfamiliar languages, such as that of the [[Lovely Duck]]'s Artifical Intelligence, [[Pyxi]].

Grey Matter's size allows him to squeeze into small spaces and he can climb walls due to microscopic pads on his skin,{{Refn|[[:File:Grey Matter Wall.PNG]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="SOTO"/> which is covered in a thin membrane that feels slimy but doesn't actually make slime.{{Refn|[[:File:Grey Matter Bandai Alien Creation Card.png]]|group = Bandai|name = card2}} He also has sharp teeth that can cause massive pain to those he bites.<ref name="ASP" />

Grey Matter is stronger than he looks, as he was strong enough to move a cleaner's bucket with mops in it<ref name="Ultimate Weapon">''[[Ultimate Weapon]]''</ref> and break a coolant pipe to freeze the [[Vreedle Brothers]].<ref>''[[So Long, and Thanks for All the Smoothies]]''</ref>

Grey Matter can breathe underwater due to having gills, making him amphibious.{{Refn|[[:File:Galvan Amphibious.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Grey Matter has a long prehensile tongue, owing to his insectivore nature, as demonstrated with [[Blukic]].<ref>''[[Evil's Encore]]''</ref> As a [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]], he also possesses a "pre-brain" which deals with all basic bodily functions,<ref>[[Rook Blonko]]</ref> as well as some mild speech and motor capability, equivalent to that of a young or foolish [[Human (Classic)|Human]].<ref>''[[For a Few Brains More]]''</ref>

Grey Matter's horizontal pupils create microscopic vision.{{Refn|group=Bandai|name=card2}}

==Weaknesses==
[[File:Problem (141).png|thumb|218x218px|Small Size]]
{{Quote|Grey Matter?! I said "muscle", not "miniscule"!|Grey Matter intending to transform into [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]].<ref name="TTH" />}}
Grey Matter's small size makes him unsuitable for physical battle, so he must outsmart his enemies in a fight. Animals like dogs and cats can be a problem, as they may see Grey Matter as a chew toy or food to them.<ref name="Ultimate Weapon" />

Being a Galvan, Grey Matter is at a massive disadvantage against the [[Nemetrix]]'s sample of an [[Omnivoracious|Omnivoracious]] due to his small size.<ref>''[[Showdown: Part 1]]''</ref>

Grey Matter is vulnerable to electricity, as demonstrated by [[Driba]].<ref name="IWT">''[[It Was Them]]''</ref>

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Grey Matter first appeared in ''[[Washington B.C.]]'', where he searched through a whole aisle of cereal boxes for a Golden '''[[Sumo Slammers (Classic)|Sumo Slammers]]''' card.
*In ''[[Hunted]]'', Grey Matter defeated [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]] and [[SixSix (Classic)|SixSix]].
*In ''[[A Small Problem]]'', the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] malfunctioned, trapping Ben as Grey Matter for most of the episode.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Grey Matter defeated one of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s [[Mechadroid|Mechadroids]] before the malfunctioning Omnitrix turned him into [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]].
**Also, Grey Matter appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[Truth]]'', Grey Matter defeated a [[Null Guardian]] and sent [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]] to the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]].
*In ''[[Grudge Match]]'', Grey Matter disabled the alien prisoners' shock implants, looked for the escape pod controls and defeated some of [[Slix Vigma]]'s [[Slix Vigma's Bodyguards|drones]] with [[Kevin 11]].
*In ''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]'', Grey Matter fought the [[Circus Freaks (Classic)|Circus Freaks]] and hid from [[Zs'Skayr]].
*In ''[[Ultimate Weapon]]'', Grey Matter snuck into a building and helped [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] to get in. He then opened a safe to retrieve the [[Mask of Ah Puch]] and escaped from [[Sir Enoch]] and the [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[They Lurk Below]]'', Grey Matter saved a drowning man from some sharks.
*In ''[[Back With a Vengeance]]'', Grey Matter appeared about eight times. Firstly, he appeared when Ben unlocked the Master Control. Then, he appeared in a photo. Later, Grey Matter escaped from Vilgax's grip while he and [[Kevin 11]] where arguing. In the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]], Grey Matter was used several times to evade Vilgax and Kevin. At the end of the episode, Ben accidentally transformed into Grey Matter, having just remembered that the Master Control was once again locked.
*In ''[[Midnight Madness]]'', Grey Matter was hypnotized into being Gwen's slave.
*In ''[[Merry Christmas]]'', Grey Matter accidentally destroyed the Rustbucket's air conditioner and later (intentionally) destroyed the [[Jinglelator]].
*In ''[[The Unnaturals]]'', Grey Matter stopped some thieves from stealing the [[Wikipedia:Liberty Bell|Liberty Bell]] and won an MP3 player in a contest.
*In ''[[Be Afraid of the Dark]]'', Grey Matter evaded Zs'Skayr and [[Dr. Viktor]], explained the former's plan to Max and Gwen, and built a [[Sun Gun]].
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''', Grey Matter attacked [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] with a hoverboard and crawled into his vest.
*In ''[[Perfect Day]]'', Grey Matter defeated a mutated [[Cash Murray (Classic)|Cash]] and [[JT (Classic)|JT]] in a dream.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''', Grey Matter escaped [[Azmuth's Father|Retaliator]] and ran back to [[Ben's House|his house]], where he was attacked by [[Carl Tennyson|Carl]] and [[Sandra Tennyson|Sandra]] before the Omnitrix switched him into [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].
*In ''[[Snack Break]]'', Grey Matter attempted to retrieve his snack in a vending machine, but reverted before he could grab it and, as a result, got stuck in the machine.

===Alien Force=== 
*Grey Matter was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Grey Matter was re-unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[So Long, and Thanks for All the Smoothies]]'', Grey Matter stopped the [[Vreedle Brothers]] from shooting at him and [[Rook Blonko|Rook]].
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Grey Matter was part of an accidental transformation chain along with [[Juryrigg]], [[Nanomech]], and [[Bloxx]].
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Grey Matter defeated [[Tyrannopede]].
*In ''[[Rad]]'', Grey Matter repaired [[Rad Dudesman|Rad]]'s [[Lovely Duck|ship]] so he and [[Ben's Team (Omniverse)|the team]] could escape.
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as Grey Matter disabled the shields on the [[Chimeran Hammer (Classic)|Chimeran Hammer]] during the events of ''[[And Then There Were 10]]''.
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Grey Matter and [[Brainfrog]] repaired each other's [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnit]][[Hero Watch|rices]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Grey Matter appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*Prior to ''[[Ken 10]]'', Grey Matter was among the intelligent aliens used by [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] to create an [[Omnitrix (Ken's Replica)|Omnitrix]] for his [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|son]]'s 10 birthday.{{Refn|[[:File:Aliens Ben 10,000 Used to Create Ken's Omnitrix.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Ken 10" />
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', Ken as Grey Matter escaped his room to help his father battle [[Devlin Levin|Devlin]] before suddenly timing out. Later, Ken as Grey Matter unlocked the Master Control offscreen before confronting [[Kevin 11,000]] and switching into [[Spitter]] to attack him.

===Gwen 10 (What-If?)===
*In ''[[Gwen 10 (Episode)|Gwen 10]]'', [[Gwen Tennyson (Gwen 10)|Gwen]] as Grey Matter was chased by a raccoon.

===[[Race Against Time Timeline]]===
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]''''', Grey Matter rewired various machines in [[Doris Dalton|Mrs. Dalton]]'s [[Le Roy's Restaurant|diner]] to throw various food at all the customers.

